From f13d8d8c5565b7024e4f80fb4b022597f18df40d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RetroStoneOS <pierrelouis.boyer@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 23:07:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] drm/sun4i: hdmi: add HDMI audio support (EXPERIMENTAL)

Add HDMI audio for the sun4i HDMI encoder (A10, A10s, A20, A31), as a
forward port of "drm: sun4i: hdmi: Add support for sun4i HDMI encoder
audio" v3 by Stefan Mavrodiev (Olimex, January 2020), which was tested
on the A20 but never merged. The register programming (audio reset and
enable, layout and channel count, channel map, channel status sampling
frequency, N/CTS, audio infoframe at 0x0a0) comes from that patch and
from the Allwinner BSP it was based on.

The structure is reworked for Linux 6.18 and for the review comments:

 - Use the generic DRM HDMI audio helpers: drm_connector_hdmi_audio_init()
   creates an hdmi-codec device for the connector (ELD control, ELD
   based hw constraints, IEC 60958 channel status, audio infoframe
   contents and jack), like vc4_hdmi does. The driver only implements
   the startup/prepare/shutdown hooks. This replaces the custom ELD
   kcontrol of v2 and the hand-built audio infoframe.

 - The CPU DAI is the HDMI audio FIFO, fed by the dedicated DMA channel
   "audio-tx" (already described in sun7i-a20.dtsi) through the generic
   dmaengine PCM, with the same bus width, burst and buffer limits as
   the tested patch.

 - The sound card is registered once at bind time, device-managed,
   instead of at every encoder enable/disable (review by Maxime Ripard).
   devm_snd_soc_register_deferrable_card() is used because the built-in
   hdmi-codec driver registers after drivers/gpu. The device drvdata
   that snd_soc_register_card() overwrites is restored afterwards, and
   the card finds the HDMI structure through card->drvdata.

 - Audio setup failures are not fatal for the display.

 - N/CTS are computed with drm_hdmi_acr_get_n_cts() from the TMDS
   character rate, and reprogrammed when the video mode changes while
   audio is running.

 - The audio infoframe is written through write_infoframe() and added
   to the packet scheduler (packet type 3, from the BSP) while audio is
   running; clear_infoframe() removes it.

 - The hdmi-codec jack follows the connector: plugged after an EDID
   read, unplugged when detect() sees HPD low.

 - Unsupported infoframe types (the SPD infoframe is generated at every
   modeset) are logged at debug level instead of as errors.

Only 16-bit stereo PCM is offered, at 32 to 192 kHz: the BSP formats
S20_3LE and S24_LE did not work in the original patch and multichannel
was never tested. As in the BSP and the original patch, the DMA
destination address is left at 0 because the dedicated DMA HDMI audio
port is selected by its DRQ type.

Chen-Yu Tsai suggested in the v3 review to drop ASoC for a plain ALSA
dmaengine card. The generic hdmi-codec route was chosen instead because
it is now the standard way for DRM HDMI drivers and brings the ELD,
channel status, infoframe and jack handling for free.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20200128140642.8404-2-stefan@olimex.com/
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20200120123326.30743-1-stefan@olimex.com/
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20200110141140.28527-1-stefan@olimex.com/
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
